{"t": 1795141135.723, "label": "Stop", "argv": [], "data": {"session_id": "01a1f6be-4fed-7ff3-886d-c2b1282b4b4c", "turn_id": "01a1f6bf-be0d-7332-9e78-104f9facc38a", "transcript_path": "/tmp/agent-tower-probes/codex-home/sessions/2026/11/19/rollout-2026-11-19T21-17-09-01a1f6be-4fed-7ff3-886d-c2b1282b4b4c.jsonl", "cwd": "/tmp/agent-tower-probes/repo", "hook_event_name": "Stop", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "permission_mode": "default", "stop_hook_active": false, "last_assistant_message": "At the edge of the island, where cliffs disappeared into fog, stood a lighthouse with a green door and a lamp that had not failed in eighty years. Mara, its keeper, knew every sound the sea could make: the hush before dawn, the slap of rain, the groan of ice against stone.\n\nOne winter night, the lamp went dark.\n\nMara climbed the spiral stairs with a box of matches, but wind swept each flame away. Below, a ship\u2019s horn called once, then again. She remembered her grandfather\u2019s stories of the old signal mirror and hurried to the lantern room.\n\nThe moon broke through the clouds. Mara angled the mirror toward it, catching a silver beam and sending it across the black water. Far out, the ship turned safely toward harbor.\n\nBy morning, the lamp was shining again. Mara polished the mirror and left it beside the window, ready for any night when the stars, or the people who watched them, might need help.\n\nQUEUED"}, "env": {"CODEX_MANAGED_PACKAGE_ROOT": "/home/demo/.nvm/versions/node/v24.10.0/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex", "CODEX_MANAGED_BY_NPM": "1", "CODEX_HOME": "/tmp/agent-tower-probes/codex-home", "AT_EMP": "cx2"}}
